<title>PERU: Peru says January sugar cane output off 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru says January sugar cane output off 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar cane production fell in January by 4.7 percent to 525,486 tonnes compared to the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Imports of sugar cane fell 15.2 percent in January to $7.171 million, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>According to the ministry's latest figures, there were no sugar cane exports in December, compared to $7.293 million in the same month in 1995. Exports last year rose 23.9 percent to $37.2 million.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
